                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Quick Verdict[/h1]\n👎 A minimalist retro platformer with an interesting presentation, but difficulty levels so extreme that it quickly becomes frustrating rather than enjoyable.\n\n[h1]Score Breakdown[/h1]\n[h3]🎮 Gameplay — 2.5/5[/h3]\nSimple platforming mechanics, but the extreme precision required on many levels makes progression feel frustrating instead of rewarding.\n\n[h3]🎨 Visuals — 3.5/5[/h3]\nMinimalist retro presentation and fake CRT aesthetic work well and give the game a distinct identity.\n\n[h3]🔊 Audio — 2.5/5[/h3]\nFunctional and fitting, but nothing particularly memorable.\n\n[h3]⚙️ Technical Performance — 5/5[/h3]\nVery light and runs perfectly smoothly.\n\n[h1]Game Profile[/h1]\n[h3]⏱️ Length[/h3]\nDeceptively very long, not because of the amount of content, but because some levels require countless attempts to complete\n\n[h3]🎯 Difficulty[/h3]\nVery hard, often requiring near pixel-perfect precision\n\n[h3]🔁 Replayability[/h3]\nLow, aside from achievement hunting\n\n[h1]Highlights & Drawbacks[/h1]\n[h3]✅ What Works[/h3]\n* Distinct minimalist CRT presentation\n* Simple and easy-to-understand mechanics\n* Extremely smooth technical performance\n\n[h3]❌ What Doesn’t[/h3]\n* Difficulty often feels excessive\n* Some levels require frustrating precision\n* Repeated failures become tiring quickly\n* Limited replay value once completed\n\n[h1]Final Thoughts[/h1]\nPrompt has an interesting visual concept and solid technical execution, but its extreme difficulty makes it hard to truly enjoy. Players specifically looking for punishing precision platformers may appreciate it more, but for most people it will likely feel more frustrating than fun.",
